WEBVTT

00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:13.144
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you think you have a healthy diet?

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:17.280
<v><b>Graziella:</b></v> Um, for the most part, I would say I have a healthy diet.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:22.090
Uh, lots of fruits and vegetables, and a little bit of chocolate, here and there.

00:00:22.729 --> 00:00:25.359
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How much sugar and salt do you eat?

00:00:25.753 --> 00:00:28.664
<v><b>Graziella:</b></v> Um, I don’t have that much salt in my diet,

00:00:28.688 --> 00:00:34.920
but with all of the fruit that I have, I would say I have quite a bit of sugar, natural sugars.

00:00:41.118 --> 00:00:42.326
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you like cooking?

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:43.779
<v><b>Kara:</b></v> I love to cook.

00:00:44.679 --> 00:00:46.385
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you think you’re a good cook?

00:00:46.592 --> 00:00:48.189
<v><b>Kara:</b></v> I do think I’m a good cook.

00:00:48.213 --> 00:00:49.853
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What’s your speciality?

00:00:50.713 --> 00:00:55.502
<v><b>Kara:</b></v> Um, my husband is Cuban, so I learned to cook Cuban food for him, so that’s my speciality.

00:01:02.178 --> 00:01:05.818
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What’s the most beautiful city you know? Why?

00:01:06.672 --> 00:01:14.152
<v><b>Maura:</b></v> Er, that’s a difficult question, but I think I’d have to say Edinburgh.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:22.086
Um, it’s very beautiful, it’s got the sea, it’s got an extinct volcano in the centre,

00:01:22.472 --> 00:01:25.822
and every street has, er, a different view.

00:01:32.571 --> 00:01:35.851
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Where are you going to go for your next holiday?

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:41.600
<v><b>Kevin:</b></v> Uh, we’ve booked that for January and we’re going to Thailand for two weeks.

00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:43.633
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Where are you going to stay?

00:01:44.172 --> 00:01:47.094
<v><b>Kevin:</b></v> We’re staying three nights in Bangkok,

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:53.259
three nights in an island called Ko Samui, and five nights in an island called Ko Tao.

00:01:54.098 --> 00:01:56.168
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How are you going to get there?

00:01:56.489 --> 00:01:59.907
<v><b>Kevin:</b></v> We are flying from Edinburgh to,

00:02:00.194 --> 00:02:05.704
uh, Dubai, Dubai to Bangkok, and then it’s another flight from Bangkok to Ko Samui,

00:02:06.184 --> 00:02:08.969
and then a ferry from Ko Samui to Ko Tao.

00:02:14.853 --> 00:02:18.761
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What’s the biggest difference between the US and the UK?

00:02:18.785 --> 00:02:24.710
<v><b>Mica:</b></v> Um, so the biggest difference between the US and the UK in New York City,

00:02:25.203 --> 00:02:28.557
uh food, very different here compared to the UK.

00:02:28.894 --> 00:02:34.027
Um, lots of burgers and pizza, and fast food and things like that.